  "summary": "Six preprints apply proteomic, transcriptomic and variant-function profiling to age-dependent changes in Huntington, TDP-43, GBA1 and ALS systems.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is high-resolution molecular profiling of neurodegeneration, with several items stressing age or disease stage. In Huntington models, R6/1 cell-type proteomics shows early excitatory synaptic protein loss and reduced glial neuronal support before motor onset, while aged TgHD minipig putamen shows age-dependent transcriptome and proteome changes, including reduced D2 neuron markers. In ALS motor cortex, neuronal somatic mutation burden is higher in younger ALS donors, with an SBS5 signature. TDP-43 work adds persistent interactome remodelling after stress granule clearance and metabolic vulnerability to lipid overload. A GBA1 assay maps lysosomal glucocerebrosidase activity for over 10,400 variants, linking function to Gaucher and Parkinson's disease. The items are not uniformly about aging.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-19"
